scripts (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `scripts format <file>` rewrites the file to the canonical layout (LF,
    no BOM, final newline, no tab or trailing space, four spaces per open
    brace); `--check` reports without writing, and the rewrite is idempotent.
  * `scripts run --no-warnings` hides the human warning block; errors still
    print, and the JSON documents keep the warnings.
  * `scripts check --module` checks a module on its own; without the flag a
    file that declares `public` is refused, and top-level statements are
    refused with SCRIPTS-MODULE-0008.
  * `scripts fmt` is removed: the command is `scripts format`.
  * NuGet restore is locked (packages.lock.json, RestoreLockedMode), and the
    gate runs shellcheck on the packaging and tooling scripts.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

scripts (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * SCRIPTS-LINT-0004 reads a literal basename inside an interpolated
    program, and no longer warns when the call already has a type or arity
    error.
  * The corpus asserts every check warning through tests/Corpus/warnings.txt.
  * The README documents provenance attestations instead of a detached
    OpenPGP signature.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000

scripts (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `scripts fmt` is renamed `scripts format`; `fmt` still runs with a
    deprecation warning until 0.3.0.
  * Build the Debian package with xz compression, so it installs on dpkg older
    than 1.21.18 (Ubuntu 22.04) and is identical across build hosts.
  * README rewritten (why, quick start, security policy); contributions are
    declined and a fork is the supported path.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000

scripts (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Block arms in a `match` expression (`=> { ...; value }`); a map literal
    arm is written `({ ... })` (breaking syntax).
  * New `process.exit_with_message`, `result.ignore_error`,
    `SCRIPTS-LINT-0013` and `SCRIPTS-LINT-0014` with `check --fix`,
    integer/float math methods, `string.find_all_regex`,
    `encoding.url_encode`/`url_decode`, `list<T>.chunked`, and the
    intrinsic `csv` module.
  * Removed `process.run_shell` (rejected statically with `SCRIPTS-TYPE-0068`).
  * .NET SDK 10.0.404 (runtime and Native AOT ILCompiler 10.0.15) with the
    November 2026 .NET runtime security fixes.
  * A `SIGINT` or `SIGHUP` ignored at startup stays ignored (POSIX convention);
    fixed a lost wake-up that could hang `parallel.run_all`.
  * Ship a `scripts(1)` manual page; the gate checks that the Debian,
    CHANGELOG and README metadata name one version before the tag.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:22:20 +0000

